{
  "id": "geo-circles",
  "chapterNumber": "7",
  "title": {
    "en": "Circles",
    "ar": null
  },
  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Circles bring their own angle and length rules: the relationship between central and inscribed angles, the right angle in a semicircle, and arcs and sectors as fractions of the whole.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Circle facts",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Circumference \\( C=2\\pi r \\); area \\( A=\\pi r^{2} \\). The inscribed angle is half the central angle on the same arc, so the angle in a semicircle is \\( 90^{\\circ} \\). An arc and sector scale by \\( \\dfrac{\\theta}{360} \\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Circumference",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( C=2\\pi r \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Area",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( A=\\pi r^{2} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Arc length",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{\\theta}{360}\\,2\\pi r \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Sector area",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{\\theta}{360}\\,\\pi r^{2} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · Arc length &amp; sector area",
          "ar": null
        },
        "canvasId": "geoSectorCanvas",
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "A circle with a shaded sector, its radius and central angle adjustable by sliders",
          "ar": null
        },
        "dataPanel": {
          "btnId": "geoSectorDataBtn",
          "panelId": "geoSectorDataPanel",
          "descId": "geoSectorDataDesc",
          "rowsId": "geoSectorDataRows",
          "caption": {
            "en": "The circle's radius, sector angle, arc length and area",
            "ar": null
          },
          "columns": [
            { "en": "quantity", "ar": null },
            { "en": "value", "ar": null }
          ]
        },
        "controls": [
          {
            "id": "geoSectorR",
            "label": { "en": "radius <b>r</b>:", "ar": null },
            "min": 1, "max": 8, "value": 4, "step": 0.5,
            "valueDisplayId": "geoSectorRval",
            "ariaLabel": { "en": "Radius r", "ar": null }
          },
          {
            "id": "geoSectorTheta",
            "label": { "en": "angle <b>θ</b>:", "ar": null },
            "min": 10, "max": 360, "value": 90, "step": 5,
            "valueDisplayId": "geoSectorThetaV",
            "ariaLabel": { "en": "Sector angle theta in degrees", "ar": null }
          }
        ],
        "readouts": [
          {
            "id": "geoSectorArc",
            "label": { "en": "arc length", "ar": null },
            "colorClass": "indigo",
            "value": "6.283"
          },
          {
            "id": "geoSectorArea",
            "label": { "en": "sector area", "ar": null },
            "colorClass": "amber",
            "value": "12.566"
          }
        ],
        "note": {
          "en": "Default r = 4, θ = 90° matches Worked example 7.B — that example rounds π to 3.14 and gets 12.56; this explorer uses exact π (≈12.566). Both a sector's arc length and its area scale by θ/360, exactly as the Reference box states.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 7.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A triangle is inscribed in a circle with one side as the diameter. Find the angle opposite that side.</p><p>The angle in a semicircle is a right angle:</p>\\[ 90^{\\circ}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 7.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find the area of a \\( 90^{\\circ} \\) sector of a circle with \\( r=4 \\). Take \\( \\pi=3.14 \\).</p>\\[ \\frac{90}{360}\\,\\pi r^{2}=\\tfrac14\\times 3.14\\times 16=12.56. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
